.TH BLOCKWRIGHT 1 2026-11-14 "Blockwright 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blockwright \- editor for ANSI and IRC block art
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blockwright
.RI [ file.ans | file.xb | file.bin | project.bwp | project-directory ]
.br
.B blockwright
.BR \-\-help | \-\-version
.br
.B blockwright \-\-screenshot
.I steps.json
.B \-o
.I dir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blockwright
draws block art on the 80-column CP437 grid: shading ramps, brushes, stamps
from a library of reusable parts, layers, generator layers driven by
scripts, and a lint that checks a piece against the craft rules.
It reads and writes ANSI (.ans with SAUCE), XBIN and BIN, exports IRC text
with mIRC colour codes and Micron pages for NomadNet, and shows how many bytes each line of a piece takes
as an IRC message.
.PP
An .ans may be CP437 or UTF-8.
Open reads it as its bytes say, or as the encoding the
.B "ANSI art, CP437"
or
.B "ANSI art, UTF-8"
filter names;
.B "File > Reopen with Encoding"
reads the open .ans again as CP437 or UTF-8.
The status bar shows the encoding Save writes the .ans in: the one it was
opened or last saved in, and for a project the one it was saved with.
Save As has a filter for each.
A UTF-8 .ans keeps every glyph but control characters, which are written as
.BR ? ;
a CP437 save that would lose glyphs a UTF-8 one keeps says so.
.PP
A project (a .bwp zip or a project directory) keeps the layers, the
generators and the saved rounds of a piece.
With a file or project argument
.B blockwright
opens it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and the commit it was built from, the Qt it runs on as a
second line, and the credits of the bundled font and icons, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " steps.json " \-o " dir"
Replay a steps file (the format
.B "blockwright-cli replay \-\-help"
gives) in the window, offscreen, and write a PNG for each step whose
.B """screenshot"""
asks for one, as
.IR NN \- name .png
or
.IR NN \- name \-before.png
and
.IR NN \- name \-after.png
for a step pictured before and after.
A screenshot is of the whole window, a dock or a widget by its object name
.RB ( """of""" ),
optionally cropped to canvas cells or to pixels
.RB ( """crop""" ),
before or after the step or both
.RB ( """when""" ),
at device pixel ratio 1 or 2
.RB ( """scale""" ;
a picture at 2 has twice the pixels each way),
with a mouse pointer at the step's last point, or its first in a picture
before the step
.RB ( """pointer""" ).
The steps file's top-level
.B """window"""
sets the window's size, 1280 x 800 without one, at either scale.
The window has default settings, the Fusion style, the bundled Noto Sans
at 10 points as its font, and fixed screens at 96 dpi that nothing in the
environment rescales, so a steps file makes the same pictures on every run.
A step that fails, a dock or widget the window doesn't have, a crop off
its target, or a pointer on a step with no point or off the picture writes
nothing and exits 1 naming the step.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/blockwright/library/
The bundled library of stamps and text styles.
.TP
.I /usr/share/blockwright/samples/
The sample projects, opened from Help > Samples and the start screen.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/blockwright/
The licence and the notices of the bundled font and icons.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blockwright-cli (1)
